  "reason": "Each FR-10 requirement maps to an assertion that fails if it is violated. (1) Content-Type problem+json: test_fr10.py:126 and the per-status checks at 157, 166, 175, 184, 193, 207, 220 and 228. (2) Required body fields: test_fr10.py:137, plus the body status equal to the HTTP status at 138. (3) No leaks in detail: test_fr10.py:148 and 288, run on a 500 whose exception message holds SQL, a traceback, a .py path and CREATE TABLE. (4) correlation_id in the X-Correlation-Id header, the body and the log: test_fr10.py:239-241 (repeated at 293-295). (5) Status-to-type mapping for 422/401/403/404/409/429/503/500: the exact dict equality at test_fr10.py:115-117. None of these assertions is inverted or trivially true. The leak check covers only the 500 path and only five fragments, so a bare directory path or a leak in a 409/422 detail would pass; that is recorded as a gap.",
